# A true result of `$isPlainHeirOf` makes a promise about the subclasses of the queried class:
# none of their prototypes holds an accessor under a name that is a field of both the object and the queried class.
# With testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime the true result is checked against the objects themselves.
# The run-time check of what is between an object and the first class prototype continues up to the prototype of the queried class.
# A class prototype on the way is queried only for an accessor, under the names of the object's own fields that the queried class also has.
# An object that belongs to no class is queried in the same way as the objects below the first class prototype.
# The check must not fail for a correct program. The cases: a field of a subclass that shadows an accessor of the library above it (`listening`); a method of a subclass under the name of a field;
# an accessor under another name; an accessor of a subclass under a name that a store has appended to the queried class alone (`extra`: every group of results queries `grown`);
# an object that the queried class itself has constructed (the result that is printed on a line by itself).
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeGuardsAndFacts: the entry check assumes that its guards hold. With that fault alone it silently returns true (BITES).
# The objects are created before the mutation. A store in a constructor after it has a run-time check of its own (for a store by name that is emitted as a store into a slot), which would fail first.
# What the check does not see: an accessor that a class declares in its body while its prototype has not reified its members yet. The check verifies the guards' half, not the walk's list.
# The proof-checks option (--aot-harden=proof-checks) ships in the hardened flavor and does not pay for this traversal.
# function Base() { this.state = 1; }
# Base.prototype.end = function () { return 1; };
# Object.defineProperty(Base.prototype, "listening", { get: function () { return 0; }, configurable: true });
# class Heir extends Base { listening = 5; }
# class Lower extends Heir { }
# class Grown extends Base { get extra() { return 3; } }
# function stamp(object) { object.extra = 5; return object; }
# function ask(object) { return $isPlainHeirOf(object, Base) ? "yes " + object.state : "no " + object.state; }            in a file of the library
